            <ArticleTitle>Autotransplantation for intractable loin pain: report of a case with long-term followup.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>389-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of autotransplantation performed 21 years ago in a patient suffering from intractable loin pain. Long-term followup, the pathogenesis of pain in regard to renal innervation and the value of autotransplantation as a form of complete sensory denervation are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
